# Three independent design proposals: skills + experience evolution
# Each vendor writes one file only. Sequential waves to avoid confusion; different output paths.
# Read docs/proposals/skills-evolution-BRIEF.md in the repo (on main after clone) — if missing, use the full task text.

1 | docs-writer | DESIGN PROPOSAL ONLY — no product code. Read docs/proposals/skills-evolution-BRIEF.md if present after checkout; it is the full brief. Goal: design basic per-role skills plus a mechanism so agents evolve from real experience, with learnings and retrospects, saving via git commit and push in TWO scopes (global in dev-agents, project-specific in product repos), at fleet scale. You are the Claude seat author. Write a complete proposal to docs/proposals/skills-evolution-proposal-claude.md covering all required sections in the brief (executive summary, basic skills catalog, runtime load model for claude/kimi/grok, experience capture, promotion/evolution, global vs project, trust/safety, retros at scale, phased rollout, success metrics, non-goals, open questions). Ground in current system facts from the brief (charters exist; unified skills tree and auto-promotion do NOT exist yet; handoffs Phase 1 parked for auto-brain). Forbidden: invent CLI flags or auth paths; edit any other skills-evolution-proposal-*.md; implement launchers. Acceptance: file exists, all required sections present, commit and push branch, draft PR if gh works else note it. Write handoff.md at repo root before exit. | feat/proposal-skills-evolution-claude

2 | plan-critic | CHARTER OVERRIDE for this task only: you are NOT reviewing a wave plan. You are a systems designer writing an independent design proposal (Grok seat). Ignore plan-critic VERDICT format except you may still be rigorous and adversarial. Read docs/proposals/skills-evolution-BRIEF.md if present. Goal: design basic per-role skills plus evolution from real experience, learnings/retros, git commit/push for GLOBAL (dev-agents) and PROJECT scopes, fleet-scale learning. Write docs/proposals/skills-evolution-proposal-grok.md with all required sections from the brief. Optimize for implementability on bash+git multi-vendor fleet (claude/kimi/grok launchers, dispatch, learnings, handoffs as raw input not auto-truth). Forbidden: invent unverified paths; edit skills-evolution-proposal-claude.md or skills-evolution-proposal-kimi.md; implement code. Acceptance: complete proposal file, commit push, draft PR if possible. Write handoff.md before exit. | feat/proposal-skills-evolution-grok

3 | web-frontend | CHARTER OVERRIDE for this task only: this is NOT a Next.js UI task. Do not edit app components. You are the Kimi seat systems designer writing a design proposal only. Read docs/proposals/skills-evolution-BRIEF.md if present. Goal: basic skills per agent role, evolution from real challenges, learnings and retrospects, persist via commit/push for GLOBAL (dev-agents repo) and PROJECT (product repo) skill stores, high-scale experience loops. Write docs/proposals/skills-evolution-proposal-kimi.md covering every required section in the brief. Be concrete about directory layout and promotion gates. Forbidden: invent auth paths or CLI flags; touch skills-evolution-proposal-claude.md or skills-evolution-proposal-grok.md; implement product UI. Acceptance: proposal file complete, commit push, draft PR if possible. Write handoff.md before exit. | feat/proposal-skills-evolution-kimi
